@startuml seq-nat-rebind
title NAT rebind healing via token re-pin (and liveness GC)

participant "NetClient\n(behind NAT)" as C
participant "Home NAT" as NAT
participant "np64-relay" as R
participant "Peers" as P

C -> NAT : frames from 192.168.1.10:41000
NAT -> R : appears as 203.0.113.7:30001
R -> R : session[token].addr = 203.0.113.7:30001

... NAT mapping expires / router rebinds (common on consumer gear) ...

C -> NAT : KEEPALIVE (token)   // every ~10 s regardless
NAT -> R : now appears as 203.0.113.7:30777
R -> R : token valid -> RE-PIN\nsession[token].addr = :30777
note right of R : any valid-token frame re-pins;\nno reconnect, no game-visible event\n(same idea as QUIC connection IDs)
R -> NAT : subsequent forwards go to :30777
NAT -> C : delivered

== liveness failure path ==
... ~30 s with no frames from a node ...
R -> R : GC node
R -> P : PEER_LEAVE fanout
note over P : games see the peer leave\nvia LIST_PEERS / EVENT irq
@enduml
